  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ZAABTA Value Addition Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Agriculture. Crops Maize rice and beans Beneficiaries: 4,321 Smallholder farmers, of whom 2284 are women Project funds will be used to acquire modern processing equipment, provide working capital to purchase grain (rice, maize and beans) from the farmers, construct a storage facility. Some of the funds will be used to improve ZAABTAs technical and management capacity through recruitment and training of staff and acquisition of accounting software......Sector: Agriculture. Crops - beans .Beneficiaries: 1000 Smallholder farmers, of whom 510 are women...Project Description: Kyazanga Farmers Cooperative Society Limited is a registered farmer owned organization based in Lwengo District. The cooperative is engaged in the multiplication of high iron bean seed for distribution to farmers through certified seed companies. The cooperative faces a number of challenges that are limiting its growth. .USADF funds used for crop finance to facilitate KFCS to purchase produce directly from farmer members at the time of harvest, which will help limit side-selling to other buyers; establishment of an input to help members gain access to quality inputs including certified seeds; procurement of drying, sorting and packing equipment; completion of a storage facility; and procurement of a truck for transportation of produce. Some of the funds will be used to improving the cooperatives technical and management capacity through recruitment and training of technical staff. ....Sector: Agriculture. Crops - beans .Beneficiaries: 1000 Smallholder farmers, of whom 510 are women...Project Description:</narrative>
  </description>
